    "Native model and FP32 ONNX outputs agree; full ONNX AP matches the training validation reference.",
    "All 240 calibration PNGs exactly match the intended preprocessing. Tested board and PC JPEG decode/RGB input arrays match pixel-for-pixel.",
    "Foreground classification logits lose confidence inside the INT8 network before Python sigmoid/NMS. Output rounding alone is too small to explain the observed score drops.",
    "Simulator layer analysis shows accumulated errors across backbone and classification layers. No single layer has been proven the unique cause.",
    "One controlled 256x160 experiment changed only quantized_algorithm normal to mmse, preserving weights and the same 60 calibration images. Recall at score .25 recovered, but localization mAP remains below FP32.",
    "FP16 RKNN has a separate small systematic box regression bias: approximately 1.9-2.6 original-image pixels per edge on 12 diagnostic images. This is not fully resolved by changing the INT8 calibration algorithm."
